he Park District says Margaret T. Burroughs Beach, often called 31st Street Beach, provides skyline views, restrooms, an ADA-accessible playground, and a public fishing dock.","source_url":"https://www.chicagoparkdistrict.com/parks-facilities/margaret-t-burroughs-beach","source_title":"Margaret T. Burroughs Beach","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Check posted swimming status and seasonal lifeguard information before entering the water; other lakefront features have separate access conditions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"armour-square-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Armour (Philip) Square Park","title":"Frame the Ballpark from the Courts","subtitle":"South Shields Avenue near 33rd Street","notes":"Head to Shields Avenue for an outdoor pause among the tennis courts, playground, and picnic areas, with the neighboring stadium in view.","short_summary":"A neighborhood recreation complex supplies an active counterpoint to the nearby stadium.","evidence_claim":"The Park District lists Armour Square Park at 3309 South Shields Avenue and documents tennis courts, a playground, picnic space, and other recreation facilities.","source_url":"https://www.chicagoparkdistrict.com/parks-facilities/armour-philip-square-park?page=1","source_title":"Armour (Philip) Square Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Park hours are 6:00 a.m.–11:00 p.m. daily; individual indoor facilities and programs may follow different schedules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"chicago-defender-building","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Chicago Defender Building","title":"Find the Defender’s Former Home","subtitle":"South Indiana Avenue near 35th Street","notes":"Pause at 3435 South Indiana Avenue to study the landmark exterior that housed the Chicago Defender during four pivotal decades.","short_summary":"A former synagogue marks the newspaper address tied to the Great Migration.","evidence_claim":"Chicago’s landmarks database says the building at 3435 South Indiana Avenue housed the Chicago Defender from 1920 to 1960 and is part of the Black Metropolis-Bronzeville Historic District.","source_url":"https://webapps1.chicago.gov/landmarksweb/web/landmarkdetails.htm?lanId=1271","source_title":"Chicago Defender Building — Chicago Landmarks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Treat this as an exterior architecture stop; the landmark listing does not establish public interior access.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"victory-monument","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Victory Monument","title":"Meet the Eighth Regiment Memorial","subtitle":"East 35th Street at Martin Luther King Drive","notes":"Stop at the 35th Street median and examine the bronze panels and soldier created to honor the Eighth Regiment’s First World War service.","short_summary":"A prominent median monument records Black military history in Bronzeville.","evidence_claim":"Chicago’s landmarks database places the Victory Monument at 35th Street and King Drive and says it honors the African American Eighth Regiment of the Illinois National Guard.","source_url":"https://webapps1.chicago.gov/landmarksweb/web/landmarkdetails.htm?lanId=1444","source_title":"Victory Monument — Chicago Landmarks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from legal pedestrian areas and use marked crossings; the monument occupies the King Drive median.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{